    // letting the integral average them drove the result toward the noise's
    // MEAN: averaging N partly-decorrelated samples divides the standard
    // deviation by about sqrt(N), so at RIPPLE_QUAD 4–6 the swing collapsed to a
    // fraction of the authored depth. Measured on the page: a full second of
    // coherent drift moved a pixel by 0.2/255, against ~0.8/255 of dust flicker
    // in the same window — the "movement" being measured was the dust.
    //
    // Held constant across the segment, the whole visible depth of one shaft
    // brightens and dims together and the variation lives ACROSS the beam
